{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-006-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/OrbitSegmentTests.cs","line":1088,"method":"SpinForward_SingleAxis_CorrectAngle","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectoryMath.Quaternions.cs:318; make PureAngleAxis return identity -> red","what_it_asserts":"That a quaternion the test itself builds from PureAngleAxis(angVel.magnitude*dt*Rad2Deg, angVel) rotates Vector3.forward by 1 radian about Y.","why_weak":"There is no production SpinForward method; the spin-forward composition lives inside ParsekFlight.ComputeOrbitalRotation (ParsekFlight.cs:22679) and is not reached. The angle formula under test is copied into the test body, so a production change to that formula cannot red this.","proposed_action":"Rename the three SpinForward_* tests to name the Pure* helpers they actually pin, and add a pure spin-forward helper in TrajectoryMath.Quaternions.cs that both ParsekFlight and the test call.","effort":"M","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-006-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/OrbitSegmentTests.cs","line":1116,"method":"SpinForward_ZeroAngVel_FallsBackToOrbitalFrame","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectoryMath.Quaternions.cs:133; invert the IsSpinning comparison -> red","what_it_asserts":"IsSpinning is false and HasOrbitalFrameRotation is true for a segment with identity OFR and zero angular velocity.","why_weak":"The name claims a fallback to the orbital frame, but no fallback code runs; the two assertions duplicate IsSpinning_DefaultSegment_ReturnsFalse and HasOrbitalFrameRotation_IdentityQuaternion_ReturnsTrue.","proposed_action":"Either delete it as a duplicate of the two predicate tests or rewrite it against the real 3-way branch once a pure spin-forward helper exists.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-006-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/OrbitSegmentTests.cs","line":1269,"method":"SpinForward_HighAngularVelocity_NoOverflow","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectoryMath.Quaternions.cs:318; make PureAngleAxis divide by an unnormalized zero axis -> red","what_it_asserts":"A quaternion built inline from a 286478 degree PureAngleAxis has no NaN or Infinity components.","why_weak":"Same inline replay as F-trajectory-orbit-006-01: the overflow the name guards belongs to the playback site, which the test never calls.","proposed_action":"Fold into the pure spin-forward helper test once that helper exists; keep the large-angle input as a boundary row.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"ParsekFlight.ComputeOrbitalRotation","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/ParsekFlight.cs","sut_line":22679,"case_kind":"state-transition","proposed_name":"ComputeOrbitalRotation_SpinningSegment_AdvancesFromBoundaryRotation","sketch":"Extract the spin-forward composition (worldAxis = boundaryWorldRot * angVel; angle = |angVel|*dt*Rad2Deg; PureAngleAxis(angle, worldAxis) * boundaryWorldRot) into a pure TrajectoryMath helper; assert the 3-way branch: spinning -> spun rotation, hasOfr only -> orbital-frame rotation, neither -> unchanged.","guards":"A regression in the spin-forward angle or axis frame that currently reds no unit test (the three SpinForward_* tests replay the formula inline).","risk":"playback"}
